{
	"_comment": "Per-area palettes read by DayNightCycle through SkyProfile. Besides the colours: sun_disc_energy is the HDR brightness of the sky-only sun disc (above the 1.2 glow threshold it blooms, so it reads as glare); sun_glow_deg / sun_glow_curve are the ProceduralSkyMaterial halo (small curve = steep falloff then a long faint tail; fog widens the halo and dims the disc on top of these); sky_curve is how tightly the horizon colour hugs the horizon (smaller = thinner band). The vale's 5.5/6.0/6.75 and 17.25/18.0/18.75 keyframes are the dawn and dusk horizon glow: a brief desaturated rose-grey band low in the sky while the dome stays dark, so sunrise and sunset ramp instead of switching. W20: the owner recorded ten minutes and could not see. Daylight sun energy was raised about 2.4x, ambient about 1.5x and fog cut to a third; night was left dark but its ambient lifted a little, because a souls game is gloomy and a game you cannot see is not gloomy, it is broken.",
